<title>USA: KP&amp;L sees Mo. coal unit back 1200 CST Thurs.</title>
<headline>KP&amp;L sees Mo. coal unit back 1200 CST Thurs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kansas City Power and Light Co's 670 megawatt Iatan coal-fired unit, shut early Tuesday, is expected to return to service within the hour, the company said Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The unit is in the process of restarting at noon today (1200 CST),&quot; a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The unit, in Weston, Mo., was shut Tuesday morning to repair a leak in a boiler feed pump.</p>
<p>The company had previously said the unit would likely restart at 0600 CST Thursday.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
